    "timeline": "Compiled Nsight timing. Collective semantics and module order are index-correlated against a separate eager module-labeled capture from the identical TorchTitan sharding plan."
  },
  "description": [
    "TorchTitan TP+SP keeps RMSNorm, residuals, and elementwise work sequence-sharded. The norm runs before each input all-gather, making the layout transition explicit instead of folding normalization into attention or MLP.",
    "Backward mirrors those layout transforms: an output-gradient all-gather precedes local backward, an input-gradient reduce-scatter returns to the sequence-sharded residual stream, and RMSNorm backward then runs on that shard.",
    "The task asks for Layer 0 only. Layer 1, embedding, output projection, distributed loss, and their measured collectives remain fixed context. TP=4 matches Qwen's four KV heads without introducing unmodeled KV replication."
  ],
